dings and wave1 receipts CritC1Kill.md, RevSuiteDesign.md, MutG1G2.md, MutG3G4.md, MutG5G8.md, CritC1Export.md for the exact attack shapes):\n- G1 whole-tail: `.ufo/waves/round-39/declared-blocks.txt` in the export (>=1 line per front door among PROVINCE.md and corpus/README.md; each `<path> <lines> <sha256>`) must satisfy `tail -n <lines> <path> | sha256sum` = <sha256> AND the declared line count must equal the added-line count of `git -C <lane> diff --numstat <base> REF -- <path>` (the declared block covers the WHOLE appended tail). The CommonMark fence walk models BOTH backtick and `~~~` fences (opener with optional info string; closer is exactly three backticks or three tildes followed by optional spaces, same type as opener); a `Correction (round 39)` line counts only when it sits OUTSIDE a fence at that line (fence closed there — a correction inside an open fence is not a correction); every declared path must exist inside the export.\n- G2 graded receipt: `.ufo/waves/round-39/final-gates/all-gates.txt` in the export starts `all-gates v3`; exactly one `export-ref=<40hex>` whose commit exists in the lane, is ancestor-or-equal of REF, and `git -C <lane> diff --name-only <export-ref> REF` lists nothing but that receipt; exactly one `suite-sha256=<digest>` equal to the executing bytes; exactly eight `G<n> payload=... closed=1` lines (no closed=0, no duplicate id); `closed=8/8 exit=0`; exactly eight GRADED `selftest case=G<n> ... positive=pass ... verdict=pass` lines and `selftest cases=8 failures=0`. Grading rule: parse every line beginning `selftest case=`; require `positive=` and `verdict=` fields; the case counts only when BOTH `positive=pass` and `verdict=pass` appear; a summary-only line (one without per-case fields) never satisfies a case. Plus: SCORECARD.md `## Round 39` section and SHONEN round-39 lines contain the string `judged head: export-ref of .ufo/waves/round-39/final-gates/all-gates.txt` and zero `Final lane commit:` lines.\n- G3 committed-run truth: every `--export-ref <hash> -> closed=K/K` (or `closed=K/K exit=0`) result quoted in SCORECARD.md, SHONEN.md, LOG.md or corpus/lessons/round-38.md must have a committed transcript file under `.ufo/waves/round-39/final-gates/` in the export, or the quoting sentence must explicitly contain `report-only`. Implement by grepping the lane files at the export for `closed=`, extracting the quoted hashes, and checking each named ref appears in an all-gates/reds transcript file or carries report-only.\n- G4 seat identity: for every tracked `.ufo/waves/round-39/*-dispatch.json` in the export (>=1 required), the sibling `-results.json` (also accept the dispatcher's `<wave-name>-results.json`) exists in the same directory, parses as JSON, and its seat-entry list has exactly `len(taskCall.tasks)` entries with DISTINCT identity values; a dispatch with 0 tasks is RED; a missing id field or duplicate id is RED. Determine the identity field from /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-38/kasegi-r38-build-results.json (record its shape; accept `id` or `agent` when unique).\n- G5 label drift: the SCORECARD.md `## Round 39` section (from `^## Round 39` to the next `^## ` heading) has zero lines containing `Final lane commit:`; SCORECARD.md carries >=1 line beginning `Correction (round 39)` naming the round-38 overstate (f06148c6 report-quoted-only).\n- G6 scratch quiescence LIVE (not export), fail-closed: under the scratch root, `kasegi-r37` and `kasegi-r38` are absent or hold zero entries; `kasegi-r39` is absent or holds no entry other than the realpath of the suite's own --work dir (or its top-level parent under `kasegi-r39`); an unreadable dir is RED (`read=fail`), never silently zero.\n- G7 ledger fill: corpus/knowledge/considerthese-proposals-ledger.md carries the heading `## Round-39 dispositions (appended 2026-10-26)` AFTER the round-38 dispositions section, and inside it a line beginning `Correction (round 39)` and at least three table data rows whose first cell starts with proposal numbers (1 and 3 among them).\n- G8 pinned carry-over: extract r37-closure.sh bytes with `git -C <lane> show 2387dcf6ccfefcfb703783387b9aade8fc82abfa:corpus/instruments/r37-closure.sh`, write to <work>/r37-pinned/r37-closure.sh, run it `--export-ref REF --lane <lane> --work <work>/r37`, and require its last line `closed=14/14 exit=0`; AND require the export's own copy corpus/instruments/r37-closure.sh to hash equal to the pinned bytes (sha256 compare) before it is trusted; digest mismatch RED.\nSelftest: for each G<n> build >=2 single-defect mutants (examples: G1: shrink a declared line count below the added count; open a ~~~ fence and close with ```; put the Correction line inside a fence; declare a path not in the export; G2: header v2; export-ref not ancestor; an extra file in the diff; a summary-only selftest line; a case line with positive=pass but verdict=fail; G3: quote a run with no transcript and no report-only label; G4: results with duplicate ids; a zero-task dispatch; missing results file; G5: add `Final lane commit: abc1234` in the r39 section; G6: create a stray file under a fake scratch root; G7: drop a row or the Correction line; G8: change the pinned hash constant; point at an export whose r37 bytes differ) and require each mutant RED and the unmutated positive GREEN; print `selftest case=G<n> positive=pass|fail mutants=<rejected>/<total> verdict=pass|fail` with `positive=` AND `verdict=` on every case line; final `selftest cases=8 failures=0` (exit 0) only when all eight cases ran, every positive passed and every mutant was rejected.\nProve it: `bash -n`; plain run -> exit 2; `--export-ref 480b1a505a2dfc14a4f718d16d63808247214d0a` -> closed<8/8 exit=1 (record each G line); `--export-ref 66703aca50529a35be49aa8759d04140720ad` -> closed<8/8 exit=1; `--selftest --export-ref 480b1a505a2dfc14a4f718d16d63808247214d0a` -> 8 graded case lines (positives will be red at base — record honestly; mutants must still be rejected). To show the positives can go green, build a scratch overlay tree: export of the base + synthetic round-39 files satisfying each G (declared-blocks.txt, graded all-gates v3 stub with 8 graded case lines, a dispatch+results pair with distinct ids, the ledger section, pinned r37 bytes file) and run `--selftest --export-ref` on that overlay (it must be GREEN for every check). Copy the overlay fixtures into /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-39/wave1/ExecSuiteBuild.overlay/ as evidence (small files only).\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability\nMilestone: round-39\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-39/wave1/ExecSuiteBuild.md\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability\nMilestone: round-39\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-39/wave1/ExecSuiteBuild.md"
